AURA AI - LAPTOP CONTROL PHASE 1
================================

IMPORTANT
- This is Phase 1: explicit text commands for basic Windows desktop actions.
- It does not yet visually understand arbitrary screen contents. Local voice commands are supported.
- It does not run arbitrary shell commands.
- Typing text only types it into the currently focused window; it does not auto-send/submit.
- Mouse fail-safe is enabled: move the mouse to the top-left corner to trigger PyAutoGUI's fail-safe.

1) BACK UP YOUR EXISTING FILE
Open your project folder:
C:\Users\sajal\OneDrive\Desktop\Aura AI\backend\app
Copy main.py to main_backup.py before replacing it.

2) COPY THE TWO FILES
Copy main.py and laptop_control.py from this bundle's app folder into:
C:\Users\sajal\OneDrive\Desktop\Aura AI\backend\app
Keep both files together in that app folder.

3) INSTALL DEPENDENCIES
Open PowerShell in:
C:\Users\sajal\OneDrive\Desktop\Aura AI\backend
Activate your existing virtual environment if needed, then run:
.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1
python -m pip install pyautogui pillow

If PowerShell says scripts are disabled, run the existing venv Python directly:
.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pip install pyautogui pillow

4) START AURA
From the backend folder run:
python -m uvicorn app.main:app --reload --port 8000

Open API docs:
http://127.0.0.1:8000/docs

5) TEST THROUGH POST /agent
Use POST /agent with JSON body:
{"message":"open Notepad"}
{"message":"open Chrome"}
{"message":"take screenshot"}
{"message":"scroll down"}
{"message":"press Ctrl+S"}
{"message":"type: Hello from AURA"}
{"message":"click at 500, 300"}

NOTE: click coordinates depend on your actual screen. First check GET /tools/laptop/status for screen dimensions.

6) DIRECT TOOL ENDPOINT
POST /tools/laptop/action examples:
{"action":"open_app","app":"notepad"}
{"action":"screenshot"}
{"action":"hotkey","key":"ctrl+s"}
{"action":"click","x":500,"y":300}
{"action":"type_text","text":"Hello"}
{"action":"scroll","direction":"down","amount":3}

Screenshots are saved to:
%USERPROFILE%\Pictures\AURA_Screenshots

7) VOICE COMMANDS
Install the voice dependencies from the backend folder:
.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pip install -r requirements-voice.txt

Keep PyAV below version 19: the installed Faster-Whisper audio decoder passes an
argument that PyAV 19 no longer accepts.

Run the API locally as described above, then open another PowerShell in the backend
folder and run:
.venv\Scripts\python.exe voice_assistant.py

Choose the microphone number shown at startup (or press ENTER to use Windows default),
then press ENTER each time you want to search or issue a command. Speak within 8 seconds;
the loop lets you make repeated requests until you stop it with Ctrl+C. Voice is
transcribed locally by faster-whisper using automatic language detection, so English,
Hindi, and Hinglish can be attempted. The API and voice_assistant.py must run on the
same computer because the API records from that computer's selected microphone. If
recognition is empty, check the printed audio level and Windows microphone privacy
permission.

SAFETY
- Only allowlisted apps can be launched. Current aliases: Chrome, browser, Edge, Notepad,
  Calculator, Paint, Explorer, and VS Code.
- Review typed text before sending it. Avoid using automation to submit forms or send messages
  until a confirmation layer is implemented.
- Do not store passwords or API tokens in chat or source code.
